/patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJII HITOSHI</name> <address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUDA SHINJI</name> <address><country>JP</country> </address> </addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUNSTAR ENGINEERING INC</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKADA MASAHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UNI SUNSTAR BV</name><address><country>NL</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJII, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUDA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUNSTAR GIKEN KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKADA, MASAHARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UNI-SUNSTAR B.V.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJII HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUDA SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKADA MASAHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJII, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUDA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKADA, MASAHARU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A bead forming method and device intended for stabler formation of hollow beads of high quality having a suitable degree of softness.  The device comprises a discharge device (10) having a double nozzle (12) consisting of inner and outer nozzles (36, 38), a gas feeder (14) for feeding gas to the discharge device, a high viscosity material feeder (16) for feeding the discharge device with a high viscosity material having fluidity in a high speed region and a high degree of shape retention in a low speed region, a manipulator (60) capable of moving the discharge device, which is attached to the front end thereof, to a desired position, and controller (22) for controlling the device in its entirety.  The discharge device (10) is moved under control along the portion to be coated of a lid (23) while discharging a gas from the inner nozzle and the high viscosity material from the outer nozzle.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé et un dispositif de formation de perles permettant de former des perles creuses de grande qualité en toute sécurité, ces perles présentant le degré de souplesse voulu. Le dispositif de cette invention comprend: un dispositif d'évacuation (10) pourvu d'une double buse (12), constituée de buses intérieure et extérieure (36, 38); un dispositif d'alimentation en gaz (14), destiné à fournir du gaz à ce dispositif d'évacuation; un dispositif d'alimentation d'une substance à grande viscosité (16), conçu pour amener au dispositif d'évacuation une substance à grande viscosité qui est fluide dans une zone à grande vitesse et présente un degré élevé de rétention de forme dans une zone à faible vitesse; un manipulateur (60) capable de faire passer dans la position souhaitée le dispositif d'évacuation, lequel est fixé à l'extrémité avant de ce manipulateur; et une commande (22) destinée à régir le dispositif dans son ensemble. Le dispositif d'évacuation (10) se déplace de manière régulée le long de la partie sur laquelle un couvercle (23) est destiné à être déposé, un gaz étant dans le même temps évacué de la buse intérieure, et ladite substance à grande viscosité éjectée de la buse extérieure.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>